# NexaTech Solutions Inc.
## Annual Financial Report
### Fiscal Years 2023, 2024, and 2025

**Report Date:** February 15, 2026  
**Classification:** Confidential - Board of Directors and Senior Leadership Only

---

## Executive Summary

NexaTech Solutions Inc. has demonstrated strong revenue growth over the three-year period from FY 2023 through FY 2025, with total revenue increasing from $42.3 million to $87.5 million, representing a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 43.8%. This growth has been driven primarily by the expansion of our subscription revenue base, which grew from $36.0 million in FY 2023 to $75.2 million in FY 2025.

Despite the impressive top-line growth, the Company has continued to operate at a net loss as we invest heavily in product development, sales and marketing, and building the infrastructure necessary to support our long-term growth trajectory. Our net loss has improved from $13.2 million in FY 2023 to $9.5 million in FY 2025, demonstrating our progress toward profitability. Our gross margins have remained consistently strong at approximately 76%, reflecting the scalability of our cloud-based software platform.

The Company successfully raised $85 million in Series C funding in September 2025, bringing our total cash and cash equivalents to $98.8 million as of the end of FY 2025. This capital provides us with a strong runway to continue executing our growth strategy and investing in innovation.

---

## Financial Performance Overview

### Revenue Analysis

NexaTech's revenue growth has been robust across both subscription and professional services segments. Our subscription revenue, which represents the recurring and predictable portion of our business, has grown at a CAGR of 44.5% over the three-year period. This growth has been fueled by both new customer acquisition and expansion within our existing customer base, as evidenced by our net revenue retention rate of 125% in FY 2025.

| **Revenue Category** | **FY 2023** | **FY 2024** | **FY 2025** | **3-Year CAGR** |
|----------------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|-----------------|
| Subscription Revenue | $36.0M | $55.3M | $75.2M | 44.5% |
| Professional Services | $6.3M | $9.5M | $12.3M | 39.7% |
| **Total Revenue** | **$42.3M** | **$64.8M** | **$87.5M** | **43.8%** |

Professional services revenue, which includes implementation, training, and consulting services, has also grown steadily, though at a slightly lower rate. This is consistent with our strategy to build a more self-service product that requires less hands-on implementation support over time.

### Product Revenue Breakdown

Our flagship product, the NexaInsight Platform, continues to be the primary driver of subscription revenue, accounting for approximately 80% of total subscription revenue in FY 2025. NexaFlow and NexaSecure, our workflow automation and security products, have also shown strong growth and are becoming increasingly important contributors to our overall revenue mix.

| **Product** | **FY 2023** | **FY 2024** | **FY 2025** |
|-------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|
| NexaInsight Platform | $28.8M | $44.2M | $60.2M |
| NexaFlow | $5.0M | $7.8M | $10.5M |
| NexaSecure | $2.2M | $3.3M | $4.5M |

### Cost Structure and Profitability

Our cost of revenue has scaled efficiently with our revenue growth. Total cost of revenue increased from $10.5 million in FY 2023 to $20.2 million in FY 2025, maintaining a relatively consistent gross margin of approximately 76%. This strong gross margin profile is characteristic of high-quality SaaS businesses and demonstrates the leverage inherent in our business model.

Operating expenses have grown significantly as we have invested in scaling the business. Research and development expenses increased from $15.2 million to $28.0 million, reflecting our commitment to product innovation and maintaining our competitive advantage. Sales and marketing expenses grew from $21.1 million to $35.0 million as we expanded our go-to-market teams and invested in brand awareness. General and administrative expenses increased from $8.5 million to $14.9 million to support the overall growth of the organization.

| **Expense Category** | **FY 2023** | **FY 2024** | **FY 2025** |
|----------------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|
| Cost of Revenue | $10.5M | $15.3M | $20.2M |
| Research & Development | $15.2M | $21.4M | $28.0M |
| Sales & Marketing | $21.1M | $29.2M | $35.0M |
| General & Administrative | $8.5M | $11.7M | $14.9M |
| **Total Operating Expenses** | **$55.3M** | **$77.6M** | **$98.1M** |

### Path to Profitability

While the Company has operated at a net loss during this period, we have made significant progress toward profitability. Our operating margin improved from -30.7% in FY 2023 to -12.1% in FY 2025. This improvement is a result of both revenue growth and increasing operational efficiency. We expect to achieve EBITDA profitability in FY 2027 as our revenue continues to scale and we gain further operating leverage.

