## Balance Sheet and Liquidity

### Asset Position

As of the end of FY 2025, NexaTech had total assets of $138.8 million, up from $47.1 million at the end of FY 2023. This growth was primarily driven by the increase in cash and cash equivalents resulting from our Series C funding round, as well as growth in accounts receivable commensurate with our revenue growth.

Our current assets totaled $122.9 million, providing strong liquidity to fund operations and growth initiatives. Accounts receivable increased from $8.2 million to $16.8 million, reflecting the growth in our customer base and revenue. Our days sales outstanding (DSO) has remained relatively stable at approximately 70 days.

| **Asset Category** | **FY 2023** | **FY 2024** | **FY 2025** |
|--------------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|
| Cash and Cash Equivalents | $28.5M | $52.3M | $98.8M |
| Accounts Receivable | $8.2M | $12.5M | $16.8M |
| Total Current Assets | $40.3M | $70.1M | $122.9M |
| Total Assets | $47.1M | $81.3M | $138.8M |

### Liabilities and Equity

Total liabilities increased from $35.5 million to $65.8 million over the three-year period. The most significant component of our liabilities is deferred revenue, which represents customer payments received in advance for subscription services. Deferred revenue increased from $21.7 million to $45.7 million, reflecting the growth in our subscription base and the strength of our recurring revenue model.

Long-term debt decreased from $5.0 million to $3.0 million as we paid down a portion of our debt obligations. Our total stockholders' equity increased significantly from $11.6 million to $73.0 million, driven by the capital raised through our Series B and Series C funding rounds.

| **Liability & Equity Category** | **FY 2023** | **FY 2024** | **FY 2025** |
|----------------------------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|
| Deferred Revenue (Current) | $18.5M | $28.2M | $38.5M |
| Deferred Revenue (Non-Current) | $3.2M | $5.1M | $7.2M |
| Total Liabilities | $35.5M | $50.1M | $65.8M |
| Total Stockholders' Equity | $11.6M | $31.2M | $73.0M |

