## Cash Flow Analysis

### Operating Cash Flow

The Company generated positive operating cash flow in all three years, with operating cash flow improving from $2.9 million in FY 2023 to $12.0 million in FY 2025. This demonstrates the underlying strength of our business model and our ability to convert revenue growth into cash generation. The improvement in operating cash flow was driven by revenue growth, improvements in working capital management, and the benefit of deferred revenue from our subscription model.

### Investing Activities

Cash used in investing activities increased from $4.5 million in FY 2023 to $8.7 million in FY 2025, primarily reflecting investments in property and equipment and capitalized software development costs. These investments are necessary to support our growth and to continue enhancing our product offerings.

### Financing Activities

The Company raised significant capital through equity financing during this period. In FY 2023, we raised $18.0 million in our Series A extension. In FY 2024, we raised $45.0 million in our Series B round. In FY 2025, we raised $85.0 million in our Series C round. These capital raises have provided us with the resources necessary to invest in growth while maintaining a strong balance sheet.

