## Key Business Metrics

### Customer Growth and Retention

Our customer base has grown significantly, from 856 customers at the end of FY 2023 to 2,147 customers at the end of FY 2025, representing a CAGR of 58.5%. Our enterprise customer segment (companies with more than 1,000 employees) has grown from 142 to 312, demonstrating our success in moving upmarket.

Net revenue retention (NRR) has remained consistently strong at over 118%, indicating that our existing customers are expanding their usage of our platform over time. This is a critical metric for SaaS companies and demonstrates the value that customers are deriving from our products.

| **Customer Metric** | **FY 2023** | **FY 2024** | **FY 2025** |
|---------------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|
| Total Customers | 856 | 1,428 | 2,147 |
| Enterprise Customers | 142 | 238 | 312 |
| Net Revenue Retention | 118% | 122% | 125% |

### Unit Economics

Our customer acquisition cost (CAC) has increased from $52,000 to $62,000 over the three-year period, reflecting the investments we are making in sales and marketing to capture market share. However, our lifetime value to CAC ratio (LTV:CAC) has improved from 2.8x to 3.5x, indicating that we are acquiring customers efficiently and that the long-term value of these customers significantly exceeds the cost to acquire them.

Average contract value (ACV) has decreased slightly from $45,000 to $37,500, primarily due to the introduction of lower-priced plans to serve the mid-market segment. However, average revenue per customer has remained relatively stable at approximately $40,000-$49,000, as existing customers expand their usage over time.

