## Operational Efficiency

### Headcount and Productivity

Total headcount increased from 300 employees at the end of FY 2023 to 537 employees at the end of FY 2025. Revenue per employee improved from $141,000 to $163,000, demonstrating increasing productivity as the organization scales. The ratio of employees per $1 million of ARR decreased from 7.8 to 6.7, indicating improved operational efficiency.

### The Rule of 40

The "Rule of 40" is a common benchmark in the SaaS industry, which states that a company's revenue growth rate plus its operating margin should exceed 40%. NexaTech's Rule of 40 score was 154% in FY 2023 (driven by very high growth), 33% in FY 2024, and 24% in FY 2025. While our score has declined as our growth rate has moderated, we remain focused on balancing growth with profitability as we scale.

